{"qid":"Q70802","names":["French Third Republic"],"title":"French Third Republic","endonym":{"native":"Troisième République","lang":"fr"},"capsule":"Established on 4 September 1870 after Napoleon III's capture at Sedan, the Third Republic became France's longest-lasting republican regime, governing for nearly seventy years. It oversaw the loss and eventual recovery of Alsace-Lorraine, colonial expansion across Africa and Indochina, and the Dreyfus Affair, which polarized French society from 1894 onward. The republic survived the First World War — during which Georges Clemenceau's leadership proved decisive — but was fatally undermined by the German invasion of May–June 1940. On 10 July 1940, the National Assembly voted by 569 to 80 to grant full powers to Marshal Philippe Pétain, dissolving itself in favor of the État français.","attestation":"Boundaries from Seshat Cliopatria (Bennett et al., Scientific Data 2025; CC BY 4.0), digitized from standard historical atlases at ~0.07° resolution. Borders are well-documented for metropolitan France; overseas colonial possessions varied considerably across the period and their exact extents depend on treaty dates used.","attestationLinks":[{"label":"Cliopatria dataset (Seshat, CC BY 4.0)","url":"https://github.com/Seshat-Global-History-Databank/cliopatria"},{"label":"Bennett et al. 2025, Scientific Data","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41597-025-04516-9"}],"citations":[{"label":"Wikipedia: French Third Republic","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/French_Third_Republic"},{"label":"Britannica: French Third Republic","url":"https://www.britannica.com/place/French-Third-Republic"},{"label":"Britannica: Dreyfus Affair","url":"https://www.britannica.com/event/Dreyfus-affair"},{"label":"Britannica: Battle of France","url":"https://www.britannica.com/event/Battle-of-France"}],"britannica":"topic/Third-Republic-French-history","cowCode":null,"wikipedia":"French Third Republic","rulers":[{"qid":null,"name":"Adolphe Thiers",